# Pitest (PIT Mutation Testing) Setup — L2 Advisory Guide

> **L2 projects:** use this guide to configure pitest manually.
> **L3 projects:** arbiter emits an enforced `gradle/pitest.gradle` fragment automatically — see AGENTS.md §Mutation Testing.

Mutation testing enforces INV-30: tests must have genuine fault-detection power, not just line coverage.
Thresholds: **80% mutation score**, **85% line coverage**. Target: domain and application layers only.

## Maven

Add to your `pom.xml` inside `<build><plugins>`:

```xml
<plugin>
  <groupId>org.pitest</groupId>
  <artifactId>pitest-maven</artifactId>
  <version>1.15.0</version>
  <configuration>
    <targetClasses>
      <param><%= locals.basePackage ? locals.basePackage + '.domain.*' : '*.domain.*' %></param>
      <param><%= locals.basePackage ? locals.basePackage + '.application.*' : '*.application.*' %></param>
    </targetClasses>
    <targetTests>
      <param><%= locals.basePackage ? locals.basePackage + '.*Test' : '*.*Test' %></param>
    </targetTests>
    <mutationThreshold>80</mutationThreshold>
    <coverageThreshold>85</coverageThreshold>
    <outputFormats>
      <outputFormat>XML</outputFormat>
      <outputFormat>HTML</outputFormat>
    </outputFormats>
    <timestampedReports>false</timestampedReports>
  </configuration>
</plugin>
```

Run: `mvn org.pitest:pitest-maven:mutationCoverage`

## Gradle

Add to your `build.gradle`:

```groovy
plugins {
  id 'info.solidsoft.pitest' version '1.15.0'
}

pitest {
  targetClasses = ['<%= locals.basePackage ? locals.basePackage + '.domain.*' : '*.domain.*' %>', '<%= locals.basePackage ? locals.basePackage + '.application.*' : '*.application.*' %>']
  mutationThreshold = 80
  coverageThreshold = 85
  outputFormats = ['XML', 'HTML']
  timestampedReports = false
}
```

Run: `./gradlew pitest`

## CI Gate

The `check-all.mjs L2` gate runs pitest automatically. Builds fail if mutation score drops below 80%.

## Why mutation testing?

Line coverage tells you which lines ran. Mutation testing tells you if tests actually verify behavior.
A test that asserts nothing can achieve 100% coverage. A mutant that survives means a test gap.
